		<h3>Daily Fiction</h3>
		<h1>Range</h1>
		<h2>By Dorthe Nors (trans. Caroline Waight)</h2>
		<div class="img-excerpt-container">
			<div class="img-container"><img src="https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/9781644454046.jpg" alt="Range"></div>
			<div class="excerpt-container"><div class="excerpt"><em>The following is from Dorthe Nors's </em>Range<em>. Nors is the author of the story collections </em>Wild Swims<em> and </em>Karate Chop<em>; four previous novels, including </em>Mirror, Shoulder, Signal,<em> a finalist for the Man Booker International Prize; and two novellas, collected in </em>So Much for That Winter<em>. She lives in Denmark.<br><br>Caroline Waight is a literary translator working from Danish, German and Norwegian. She has translated a wide range of fiction and nonfiction, with recent publications including </em>The Lobster's Shell<em> by Caroline Albertine Minor, </em>Island<em> by Siri Ranva Hjelm Jacobsen and </em>The Chief Witness<em> by Sayragul Sauytbay and Alexandra Cavelius. She lives and works near London.</em></div></div>
